tribe in Pueblo to be able to join in,

00:09:57.412 --> 00:10:02.533
to have a safe space to talk about and
find out more about psilocybin and the

00:10:02.533 --> 00:10:04.240
direction that it's going.

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:09.439
And so that we can hear from people the
cultural and historical considerations

00:10:09.439 --> 00:10:12.920
that we need to ensure that we're that
we're honoring.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:15.400
And so we have asked for that.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:20.360
And our hope is that we see that meetings
getting set up shortly.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:24.185
However, again,
we do have to work through our tribal

00:10:24.185 --> 00:10:24.640
liaison.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:28.280
And so we'll see as soon as we have
information, we'll put that on out.

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:32.674
And then as far as other information,
some of the things that we've talked

00:10:32.674 --> 00:10:37.013
about in some of the previous meetings or
what we really need to do is start honing

00:10:37.013 --> 00:10:40.320
in on what are the requirements with
regard to the equity fund.

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:44.827
So for example,
are we looking initially just at things

00:10:44.827 --> 00:10:45.960
such as income?

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:48.600
How does geography play into that?

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:53.720
How does membership and otherwise wise
marginalized communities play into that?

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:57.040
How do we help in ensure that there's
access?

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:02.643
And So what we really need to start doing
is start honing that in and making some,

00:11:02.643 --> 00:11:05.745
you know,
recommendations so that when it comes

00:11:05.745 --> 00:11:10.980
time for that particular set of rules,
we actually are able to say these are the

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:16.280
criteria for individuals to be able to,
you know, to be able to access that fund.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:20.200
And so, so that's really,
I think the next step.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:23.373
And,
and we did have some sort of propositions

00:11:23.373 --> 00:11:28.506
with regard to that of ensuring things
such as travel and transportation for

00:11:28.506 --> 00:11:32.173
individuals,
which I take to also include lodging when

00:11:32.173 --> 00:11:33.640
people are travelling.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:40.310
Methods and ways that the program could
potentially fund for either mobile or,

00:11:40.310 --> 00:11:43.964
you know,
for providers to travel into areas rather

00:11:43.964 --> 00:11:48.040
than the patients traveling out of areas
to the provider.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:51.480
So ensuring that we have that,
that's a big part of access as well.

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:57.369
And then some of the other aspects for
once we have locked down and we don't

00:11:57.369 --> 00:12:00.476
have this yet,
but once we know how much could

00:12:00.476 --> 00:12:05.500
potentially be covered through Medicaid
and through insurance as far As for

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.880
billing issues or billing questions.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:11.467
Once we have that,
then what kind of income requirements

00:12:11.467 --> 00:12:16.400
would there be for individuals to be able
to reach or to be able to access the fund?

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:21.801
And we've talked about various levels,
but I think we need to start honing in a

00:12:21.801 --> 00:12:27.115
little bit on those levels because that's
kind of the easy part in some ways to be

00:12:27.115 --> 00:12:32.109
able to say, if someone's at, for example,
200% of the federal poverty level,

00:12:32.109 --> 00:12:35.374
how much will the program then fund the,
you know,

00:12:35.374 --> 00:12:39.215
their treatment if they're at at poverty
level or below it,

00:12:39.215 --> 00:12:41.200
how much will the program fund?

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:45.440
And sort of setting up a chart with that
to, to really sort of have that.

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:50.135
Is it going to be an all or nothing where,
for example, we say,

00:12:50.135 --> 00:12:53.240
if somebody is at 400% of the poverty
level.

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:56.376
And by the way,
these numbers where I'm saying that

00:12:56.376 --> 00:13:01.080
percentages are just ones to sort of for
us to starting point to, to discuss.

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:04.960
They're not anything written in stone in
any way, shape or form.

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:08.516
But so for example,
if someone's at 400% of the poverty level,

00:13:08.516 --> 00:13:11.560
are we just going to then fund the
treatment at that point?

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:13.600
Or will it be a percentage?

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:19.462
Will it be simply that we turn around and
say and then anyone over that level or

00:13:19.462 --> 00:13:24.014
whatever level we decide on,
anyone over that level then you know,

00:13:24.014 --> 00:13:26.799
is there no funding allowed or available?

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:29.040
You know,
so it's about those sort of things.

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:32.600
Do we do it graduated or does it become
just a cut off?

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:35.729
If it is graduated or a cut off either
way,

00:13:35.729 --> 00:13:38.320
what are those requirements going to be?

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:42.190
And then from there,
one of the things that we'll have to

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:46.709
determine is how much information are
those individuals going to have to

00:13:46.709 --> 00:13:49.000
provide showing what their income is?

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:52.320
Do we go with something simple, which is,
by the way,

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:56.653
has happened with many programs where
they simply say the previous year's tax

00:13:56.653 --> 00:13:59.320
returns and that helps to determine that
level?

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:04.412
Or do we go into more depth and say we
need to have more information about right

00:14:04.412 --> 00:14:09.002
now because people's income levels can
change from one year to the next and

00:14:09.002 --> 00:14:13.170
because it's a full year on that
somebody's tax return from the year

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:17.640
before may not reflect where they are now,
whether it is higher or lower.

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:20.040
So these are things that we need to
determine.

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:23.895
Some of it, however,
is going to also be dependent upon the

00:14:23.895 --> 00:14:28.716
ability of the program and the resources
the program has to be able to actually

00:14:28.716 --> 00:14:29.440
review that.

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:33.207
So for example,
if we said it would be based on income

00:14:33.207 --> 00:14:36.898
now and just as a,
a few examples of what they do in certain

00:14:36.898 --> 00:14:41.617
other programs that would include things
like what is rent statement so or a,

00:14:41.617 --> 00:14:45.792
a rental lease so that we can see how
much is going out for housing,

00:14:45.792 --> 00:14:48.877
because there's a very different approach
as well,

00:14:48.877 --> 00:14:53.415
looking at it from a standpoint of what
is your income versus what is your

00:14:53.415 --> 00:14:53.960
expenses.

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:56.720
And so we have to take that into
consideration as well.

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:59.511
So for example,
we look at what are your last two or

00:14:59.511 --> 00:15:02.160
three pay stubs, What are your, you know,
your rental.

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:06.262
Does that then mean that people are not
going to want to submit it and therefore

00:15:06.262 --> 00:15:09.249
it might miss out because,
and rightfully so, they say, well,

00:15:09.249 --> 00:15:12.814
why does the Department of Health,
why are they being so nosy and want to

00:15:12.814 --> 00:15:15.320
see what all my income is and those sort
of things?

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:19.533
So we have to think about some of those
aspects as well because there's also a

00:15:19.533 --> 00:15:23.640
certain amount of stigma that is attached
with with many of these questions.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:28.601
And so do we go with something simpler
like the previous year's tax returns,

00:15:28.601 --> 00:15:33.442
knowing that there might be issues and
maybe putting in if somebody's income has

00:15:33.442 --> 00:15:36.371
increased,
maybe not worrying about that so much

00:15:36.371 --> 00:15:39.240
because of some of the potential stigma
issues.

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:43.235
But if it's decreased,
having an alternate path that someone

00:15:43.235 --> 00:15:47.840
then could do these other things that may
be quite frankly more invasive,

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:50.640
but help them in order to be able to
ensure.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:55.649
So going with something as the first line
being what are your previous year's tax

00:15:55.649 --> 00:15:58.546
returns,
